## Experience and Lessons
|Case|:user_login  
Pseudocode:  
```python
FUNCTION login_user(username, password):
    IF users.txt EXISTS:
        READ users.txt line by line
        FOR each line:
            SPLIT line into stored_user, stored_pass
            IF stored_user == username AND stored_pass == password:
                RETURN True
    RETURN False

ROUTE /login (GET/POST):
    IF POST request:
        EXTRACT username, password from form
        IF login_user(username, password) == True:
            STORE username in session
            REDIRECT to /recommendations
        ELSE:
            RENDER login.html WITH error="Invalid credentials"
    ELSE:
        RENDER login.html
```
Key Libraries:  
- Flask (`session`) 每 Manages user sessions.  
- File I/O (`users.txt`) 每 Stores user credentials in plaintext.  

---

2. |Case|:input_travel_preferences  
Pseudocode:  
```python
FUNCTION save_preferences(username, budget, activities, climate):
    IF preferences.txt EXISTS:
        READ all lines EXCEPT those matching username
    APPEND new preference line (username|budget|activities|climate)
    WRITE all lines back to preferences.txt

ROUTE /preferences (GET/POST):
    IF user NOT logged in:
        REDIRECT to /login
    IF POST request:
        EXTRACT budget, activities, climate from form
        CALL save_preferences(username, budget, activities, climate)
        REDIRECT to /recommendations
    ELSE:
        RENDER preferences.html
```
Key Libraries:  
- Flask (`request`) 每 Handles form submissions.  
- File I/O (`preferences.txt`) 每 Stores user preferences.  

